\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {II}{\ignorespaces Scalar charge $D$ of the anchor solutions ($\eta _0=1$, $\omega _\infty =0.5$) against Ref.~\cite  {chew2016}. Along each fixed-$\gamma $ family, $\omega _\infty $ rises, turns over and descends, so $\omega _\infty =0.5$ is reached twice; the published values sit on the post-turnover branch. Our values are grid-converged to the digits shown; the $\gamma =2$ family continued to $J=172$ confirms no third crossing exists. The two positive-$\gamma $ offsets are the published values' finite-difference error, growing with $\gamma $; the pre-turnover branch is new.}}{7}{table.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:anchors}{{II}{7}{Scalar charge $D$ of the anchor solutions ($\eta _0=1$, $\omega _\infty =0.5$) against Ref.~\cite {chew2016}. Along each fixed-$\gamma $ family, $\omega _\infty $ rises, turns over and descends, so $\omega _\infty =0.5$ is reached twice; the published values sit on the post-turnover branch. Our values are grid-converged to the digits shown; the $\gamma =2$ family continued to $J=172$ confirms no third crossing exists. The two positive-$\gamma $ offsets are the published values' finite-difference error, growing with $\gamma $; the pre-turnover branch is new}{table.2}{}}
